From 41de8f9146f55b6fa7a31050a9b2096425cc26ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fadigah Ijesse <you@example.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 15:11:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix navbar responsive scaling and add mobile hamburger menu

- navbar.css: replace fixed breakpoint sizing with clamp()-based
  fluid sizing so the navbar scales smoothly instead of overlapping
  buttons at in-between viewport widths / browser zoom levels; fix
  stray closing brace; replace hardcoded-offset mobile panels with
  a single robust .mobile-menu dropdown anchored via top:100%
- navbar.js: implement hamburger open/close, icon swap, close on
  link click / outside click / Escape / resize back to desktop
- index.html, articles.html, article.html: add hamburger button
  markup and wrap nav links + buttons in .mobile-menu; include
  navbar.js on articles.html and article.html (previously missing)
---
